From: ShareOS <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] http: no abort for clients on a Unix socket

name_from_addr() ends the program with event_errx() when getnameinfo()
fails. musl's getnameinfo() does not know AF_UNIX, so the first request
to an evhttp server bound to a Unix socket (Transmission's
rpc-bind-address "unix:...") killed the server. Name such peers
"unix" port "0" instead (libevent 2.2 handles AF_UNIX the same way).

--- a/http.c	2026-10-21 08:22:49.050462739 +0200
+++ b/http.c	2026-10-21 08:22:49.069224468 +0200
@@ -4360,6 +4360,16 @@
 	char strport[NI_MAXSERV];
 	int ni_result;
 
+#ifdef AF_UNIX
+	/* a peer on a Unix socket has no host or port; getnameinfo() of musl
+	 * refuses AF_UNIX, and the error below would end the whole program */
+	if (sa->sa_family == AF_UNIX) {
+		*phost = mm_strdup("unix");
+		*pport = mm_strdup("0");
+		return;
+	}
+#endif
+
 #ifdef EVENT__HAVE_GETNAMEINFO
 	ni_result = getnameinfo(sa, salen,
 		ntop, sizeof(ntop), strport, sizeof(strport),
